.TH ZERODDS-WS-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "2026-05-06" "1.0.0-rc.1" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-ws-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-ws-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/ws-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the WebSocket bridge daemon binds DDS topics
to WebSocket URLs. Top-level keys
.BR participant ", " websocket ", " routes ", " logging ", " observability .
.SH KEYS
.SS participant
.TP
.B domain_id
Integer DDS-Domain-ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B qos_profile
Profile name resolved by the QoS-Library, e.g.
.IR builtin/reliable_keep_last_10 .
.SS websocket
.TP
.B bind
Listen address, e.g.
.IR "0.0.0.0:8080" .
.TP
.B tls.enabled
Boolean. When true,
.BR cert " and " key
must point to PEM material readable by user
.IR zerodds .
.TP
.B origin_allowlist
List of regexes matched against the WS Origin header. Empty list = allow all.
.TP
.B max_message_bytes
DoS-cap on individual frames; default
.IR 1048576
(1 MiB).
.TP
.B ping_interval_secs
Send ping every N seconds.
.TP
.B pong_timeout_secs
Drop client when no pong within this window.
.SS routes (list)
Each entry has:
.TP
.B dds_topic
Topic name on the DDS side.
.TP
.B type
Fully-qualified IDL type, e.g.
.IR demo::Chat::Message .
.TP
.B ws_path
HTTP path the client connects to, e.g.
.IR /chat .
.TP
.B direction
One of
.IR dds_to_ws ", " ws_to_dds ", " bidirectional .
.SS logging
.TP
.B level
trace | debug | info | warn | error.
.TP
.B format
.I json
(machine readable, recommended for journald) or
.IR pretty .
.TP
.B destination
.I journal " | " "file:/path"
.SS observability
.TP
.B metrics_bind
Prometheus listen address.
.TP
.B otlp_endpoint
HTTP endpoint for OTLP export, empty disables.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/ws-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-ws-bridged (1),
.BR zerodds-xmlc (1).
